!!id:"https://schemas.example.com/2026/40/orders/orders-api-1.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/2026/40/io/ltr8/http/http.tn"
!!import:"https://schemas.example.com/2026/40/orders/orders-1.tn"
@doc:"""
  Both: the protocol of orders-1.tn, and the http projection that binds it. Every endpoint is a `!http.binding`
  naming an exchange and borrowing its signature. The exchange is a reference the resolver judges, a
  qualified name through the protocol's entry, its `exchanges` field and its key -- `orders.exchanges.place_order`
  -- so a misspelt exchange fails at load. What a binding adds is the placement of that exchange's one request
  record over the HTTP request, which is where the two views are allowed to look different:

    POST   /orders        new_order   { order  idempotency_key }  order unwrapped as the body,
                                                                  idempotency_key as Idempotency-Key
    GET    /orders/{id}   order_ref   { id }                      id from the path
    GET    /orders        order_query { status  page  page_size } all three in the query (a GET's remainder)
    DELETE /orders/{id}   order_ref   { id }                      id from the path; nothing left over

  `binds: [orders]` is a claim the reader holds the projection to: every exchange of `orders` has a binding
  here, or an exemption in `not_bound` giving the reason it does not. Each name in it is a reference the
  resolver judges, so a protocol nothing declares fails at load too.
  """
!schema {
  orders_http => !http.projection {
    binds: [orders]
    resources: {
      "/orders" => {
        @service.summary:"Place an order."
        @doc:"""
          Accepts a new order and confirms it. Repeating the request with the same Idempotency-Key returns the
          original confirmation rather than placing a second order.
          """
        POST => !http.binding { exchange: orders.exchanges.place_order  status: 201
                                body: order  headers: { idempotency_key => "Idempotency-Key" } }
        @service.summary:"Search orders."
        GET  => !http.binding { exchange: orders.exchanges.list_orders }
      }
      "/orders/{id}" => {
        GET    => !http.binding { exchange: orders.exchanges.get_order }
        DELETE => !http.binding { exchange: orders.exchanges.cancel_order  status: 204 }
      }
    }
  }
}
